BOE wants a share of the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/macbook-ultra/">OLED</a> supply chain for Apple's <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/07/31/ipad-air-could-be-redesigned-next-year/">next iPad Air</a>, aiming to land a secondary sourcing role behind primary supplier Samsung Display, according to a report from South Korea's <a href="https://www.thelec.net/news/articleView.html?idxno=12961"><em>The Elec</em></a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2025/10/m3-ipad-air-mint.jpeg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1024964" /><br/>
Sources cited by <em>The Elec</em> say the Chinese panel maker is building out its <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad-air/">iPad Air</a> &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; effort at its B12 fab in Chongqing, home to BOE's sixth-generation &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; production line, ahead of the launch of a redesigned &zwnj;iPad Air&zwnj; that isn't expected to launch until the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/04/16/2027-ipad-air-much-better-display/">first half of 2027</a>. Samsung Display already holds the lead supply role for that panel and is on track to begin ramping production toward the end of this year or the start of next, as <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/04/15/report-ipad-air-to-gain-oled-display-next-year/">previously reported</a>.<br/>
<br/>
BOE still has to clear Apple's qualification process. Samples reportedly still need to be submitted for evaluation, and a verdict on whether the company wins any commercial orders is not expected until closer to the end of the year. Even a favorable outcome may only translate into modest volume at first, with output confined to &zwnj;iPad Air&zwnj; units destined for the Chinese market or to refurbished devices, rather than the entire global launch.<br/>
<br/>
The sources put BOE's qualification decision at some point in November or December, noting Apple typically finalizes production approval just one to two months ahead of mass production actually starting. Should BOE fall short of that bar, Samsung Display will end up carrying the entire initial production run by itself.<br/>
<br/>
Becoming a supplier for the &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; &zwnj;iPad Air&zwnj; would be a meaningful expansion for BOE, which has experience providing &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; panels for the iPhone, but has struggled to break into larger &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; products. Samsung Display and LG Display have held onto that ground in tablets specifically, and BOE has lost, rather than gained, footing elsewhere in Apple's &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; lineup recently; its utilization on Apple-dedicated lines reportedly slid from roughly 82% in 2024 to about 48% earlier this year as Apple is set to <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/06/25/ipad-mini-oled-panel-mass-production-starts/">lean on Samsung instead</a> for the upcoming &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad-mini/">iPad mini</a>.<br/>
<br/>
The redesigned &zwnj;iPad Air&zwnj; is expected in 11 inch and 13 inch sizes, with a hybrid &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; panel pairing a glass substrate with thin film encapsulation, a single stack RGB emissive layer, and an LTPS backplane, with a refresh rate of 60Hz. That keeps it below the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad-pro/">iPad Pro</a>'s tandem stack &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; panel on cost, while still moving the &zwnj;iPad Air&zwnj; away from an LCD.<br/>
<br/>
BOE is also reportedly pursuing a secondary supplier role for Apple's &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macbook-pro/">MacBook Pro</a> from its 8.6 generation B16 fab in Chengdu, but persistent yield problems there make commercial shipments to Apple unlikely soon. Industry sources do not expect BOE to enter that supply chain until sometime after 2028.<div class="linkback">Related Roundup: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad-air/">iPad Air </a></div><div class="linkback">Tags: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/boe/">BOE</a>, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/oled/">OLED</a>, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/the-elec/">The Elec</a></div><div class="linkback">Buyer's Guide: <a href="https://buyersguide.macrumors.com/#iPad-Air">iPad Air (Buy Now)</a></div><div class="linkback">Related Forum: <a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/forums/ipad.137">iPad</a></div><br/>This article, &quot;<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/11/ipad-air-oled-panel-orders-could-be-split-with-boe/">iPad Air OLED Panel Orders Could Be Split With BOE in 2027</a>&quot; first appeared on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com">MacRumors.com</a><br/><br/><a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/ipad-air-oled-panel-orders-could-be-split-with-boe-in-2027.2486729/">Discuss this article</a> in our forums<br/><br/>